    "details": "Cherry blossom peaks first in the far south and moves north over about three months. The season has its own name in each country: in China yinghua (樱花), in Japan sakura (桜) with hanami (花見) for the viewing parties, in Korea beotkkot (벚꽃). Dates are rough typical peaks from general knowledge, not a forecast; they shift by a week or two each year, and the area table is meant to be corrected. China is a very rough starter.",
